  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_001: RNA-only/PCA/singleprofile at 48.5% accuracy), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Testing config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image contribution without confounding from fusion or multiprofile aggregation, and uses the simplest image encoder for a clean comparison against the RNA baseline. If image accuracy is substantially higher or lower than 48.5%, it immediately clarifies whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing and which modality should anchor the model. If it is similar, the bottleneck is likely task difficulty rather than modality choice, redirecting effort toward RNA encoder improvements. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design axis (modality value) before committing limited budget to the much larger multimodal configuration space."
}

